#
# Conformance case: foundation/holon-projection
# AC: holon kernel — the lossy unary logic:Holon projection (issue #704, C1).
#
# Holon-ness is contextual (the canonical construct is the relational
# logic:HolonicPosition); logic:isHolon is its lossy unary projection: an entity
# that, within a holarchy, is BOTH a proper part of some whole AND itself has a
# proper part. A strict-parthood chain Engine ⊏ Car ⊏ Fleet exercises it:
#   * ex:Car    — a proper part of ex:Fleet AND a whole of ex:Engine → logic:isHolon.
#   * ex:Fleet  — the root whole (no whole above it) → NOT a holon.
#   * ex:Engine — an atomic leaf (no proper part below it) → NOT a holon.
# It also exercises logic:overlaps: a proper part overlaps its whole (both
# directions), and a whole with a proper part overlaps itself via that part.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the parthood edges
# are duplicated there in the named world ex:schema; these are the program axioms.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/holon-projection/> .

# Schema: a three-level strict-parthood chain (also world facts in input.nq).
ex:Engine logic:properPartOf ex:Car .
ex:Car    logic:properPartOf ex:Fleet .
